#
# Table salt (sodium chloride, halite): a 4 x 4 x 4 piece of the rock salt lattice, 32 Na+ and 32 Cl- ions, built for the Cell and Molecule Explorer.
# Ion spacing a/2 = 2.82005 angstroms from the measured cell edge a = 5.6401 angstroms, Crystallography Open Database 9003308
# (Walker et al., American Mineralogist 89, 204, 2004; halite at 25 C, 0 kbar; COD data CC0). No bonds: the ions are held by charge, not shared electrons.
# Ion radii for drawing (OpenStax Chemistry 2e 10.6): Na+ 1.02, Cl- 1.81 angstroms.
#
_chem_comp.id                     NACL
_chem_comp.name                   'SODIUM CHLORIDE CRYSTAL PIECE'
_chem_comp.type                   NON-POLYMER
_chem_comp.formula                'Cl Na'
_chem_comp.pdbx_formal_charge     0
_chem_comp.three_letter_code      NACL
_chem_comp.pdbx_ideal_coordinates_missing_flag N
